<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_rate" target="europe_political_shift::far_right_support" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Visible increases in weapons shipments and military aid become focal points for far-right campaigns framing governments as prioritizing foreign security over domestic needs, mobilizing voters and boosting radical-right vote share.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">europe_political_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_rate" target="global_bond_repricing::short_term_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Large, rapid arms deliveries financed by donor governments prompt accelerated short-term fiscal issuance (e.g., T-bills) and draw on domestic funding backstops, increasing near-term supply of short-duration government paper and upward pressure on short-term funding costs.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_repricing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_rate" target="gulf_maritime_conflict::conflict_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Increases in Western arms deliveries to Ukraine prompt Russia and its regional partners to accelerate supply and training for proxies (e.g., Houthi, Hezbollah) and to authorize more aggressive maritime harassment, raising kinetic and proxy strike activity in the Gulf theatre.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">gulf_maritime_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_rate" target="us_china_tech_trade::export_controls_tightnes" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Large, visible arms transfers that incorporate dual‑use electronics and guidance systems raise concerns about technology diversion and rapid militarization, prompting regulators to extend and tighten export restrictions on advanced semiconductors and AI components to China.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
