  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An increased flow of semiconductors into European supply chains reduces shortages and production disruptions, which voters interpret as effective government/industry crisis management and thereby raises trust in political institutions.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d39">europe_political_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_trade::semiconductor_prod_rate" target="global_bond_repricing::portfolio_reallocation" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">A decline in semiconductor production (i.e., a negative change) quickly compresses tech earnings prospects and supply‑chain visibility, triggering accelerated investor reallocations out of tech equities into safer assets and thus a higher portfolio reallocation rate (conversely, an increase in production dampens such reallocation).</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_repricing</data>
</edge>
