<edge source="global_bond_repricing::funding_stress" target="europe_political_shift::policy_uncertainty" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute short-term funding stress compels central banks and treasuries to deploy emergency liquidity operations, ad hoc guarantees and regulatory forbearance, producing opaque, fast-moving interventions that raise perceived unpredictability about future policy directions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">europe_political_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::funding_stress" target="gulf_maritime_conflict::shipping_throughput_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute short‑term funding stress causes banks and brokers to curtail trade‑finance lines and require higher margins for letters of credit, directly forcing exporters/importers to delay or cancel shipments and reducing transit volume through Gulf chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">gulf_maritime_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::funding_stress" target="gulf_maritime_conflict::maritime_security_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Funding strains compress liquidity at insurers and private maritime security firms, prompting coverage withdrawals or sharply higher war‑risk premiums that leave commercial vessels more exposed and raise measured maritime security risk.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">gulf_maritime_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::funding_stress" target="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Elevated short-term funding stress tightens trade and export finance, raises working-capital costs and margin calls for defence manufacturers and logistics providers, causing delivery delays and reducing the volume and cadence of arms shipments into the theater.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::funding_stress" target="us_china_tech_trade::ai_infra_investment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising short‑term funding stress raises rollover and repo costs for cloud operators and colo providers, forcing near‑term capex cuts and delays in procurement of servers/accelerators and thereby reducing AI infra deployments.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
